<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Khalji dynasty of Bengal</h1><p class="st-meta">1204 CE – 1227 CE · capital Lakhnauti</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Muslim regime in Bengal, founded by Bakhtiyar Khalji's conquest of the Sena capital and ruled from Lakhnauti.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiyar-khalji">Muhammad Bakhtiyar Khalji</a>, a Turkic-Afghan commander serving the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ghurid-sultanate">Ghurids</a>, raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> and then, around 1204, surprised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sena-dynasty">Sena</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmana-sena">Lakshmana Sena</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabadwip">Nadia</a>. He established a capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Lakhnauti</a> (Gaur) and ruled northern and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> with his Khalji officers, nominally under the Ghurid sultans.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Khalji chiefs governed as a military aristocracy, dividing land among commanders and founding mosques and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiyar-khalji">Bakhtiyar</a> died after a disastrous expedition towards <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tibet-1912-1951">Tibet</a> around 1206. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwaz-khalji">Iwaz Khalji</a>, who took the title Ghiyath al-Din, was the most effective ruler: he built roads and embankments, created a river fleet and struck coins in his own name.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> sent his son Nasir al-Din Mahmud against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwaz-khalji">Iwaz</a>, who was defeated and killed in 1227. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> became a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Lakhnauti</a>, until independent sultans arose again, leading eventually to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bengal-sultanate">Bengal Sultanate</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1204 CE – 1227 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.66%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1204 CE – 1227 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lakhnauti</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad Bakhtiyar Khalji, Ali Mardan Khalji, Iwaz Khalji</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khaljis of Lakhnauti</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1216&amp;focus=khalji-dynasty-of-bengal" aria-label="Khalji dynasty of Bengal on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6808 1371 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khalji dynasty of Bengal lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7358 1570h0M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7128 1627h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7128 1627h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=1216&amp;focus=khalji-dynasty-of-bengal">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
